step Riding at 40
  only Orc,!Warlock
  zone Orgrimmar
  when level>=40
  when !skill Riding 1
  tip Riding needs level 40 and costs 100 gold; learning it gives you a mount, and the Riverglades after Stranglethorn are a long walk without one. Take the zeppelin from Grom'gol's tower to Orgrimmar: Kildar teaches Orcs in the Valley of Honor, by Ogunaro Wolfrunner's kennel (wolves 20 gold each). Then the zeppelin back to Grom'gol. Short of gold? Skip this step: the Feralas guide passes Orgrimmar again at about 45.
  train 4752                            -- Kildar, riding trainer

step Riding at 40
  only Troll,!Warlock
  zone Durotar
  when level>=40
  when !skill Riding 1
  tip Riding needs level 40 and costs 100 gold; learning it gives you a mount, and the Riverglades after Stranglethorn are a long walk without one. Take the zeppelin from Grom'gol's tower to Orgrimmar and go south down the Durotar road to Sen'jin Village: Xar'Ti teaches Trolls there, with Zjolnir's raptors (20 gold each). Then back to the zeppelin for Grom'gol. Short of gold? Skip this step: the Feralas guide passes Orgrimmar again at about 45.
  train 7953                            -- Xar'Ti, riding trainer

step Riding at 40
  only Tauren
  zone Mulgore
  when level>=40
  when !skill Riding 1
  tip Riding needs level 40 and costs 100 gold; learning it gives you a mount, and the Riverglades after Stranglethorn are a long walk without one. Take the zeppelin from Grom'gol's tower to Orgrimmar, fly to Thunder Bluff and ride down to Bloodhoof Village: Kar Stormsinger teaches Tauren there, with Harb Clawhoof's kodos (20 gold each). Then fly back to Orgrimmar for the Grom'gol zeppelin. Short of gold? Skip this step: the Feralas guide passes Thunder Bluff again at about 45.
  train 3690                            -- Kar Stormsinger, riding trainer

step Riding at 40
  only Skyborne,!Warlock
  zone Zephras Isle
  when level>=40
  when !skill Riding 1
  tip Riding needs level 40 and costs 100 gold; learning it gives you a Galestrider, and the Riverglades after Stranglethorn are a long walk without one. Take the zeppelin from Grom'gol's tower to Orgrimmar and fly to Thunder Bluff: the skyboat to Zephras Isle leaves the cliffs south of Skywatcher Plateau, north of Thunder Bluff, about every five minutes, and Genn Fairweather teaches Skyborne at the Fairweather Stables in Valanaar. Then back to Orgrimmar for the Grom'gol zeppelin. Short of gold? Skip this step: the Feralas guide passes Orgrimmar again at about 45.
  train 265756                          -- Genn Fairweather, riding trainer, at the Fairweather Stables in Valanaar

